   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the private housing finance law, in relation to increasing the\nbonding authority of the New York city housing development corporation",
    "basePrintNo": "S10442",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10442-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §656, Priv Hous Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Private Housing Finance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10442\n\nSPONSOR: KAVANAGH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the private housing finance law, in relation to increas-\ning the bonding authority of the New York city housing development\ncorporation\n\n1Section 1. Paragraph c of subdivision 1 of section 656 of the private\nhousing finance 2 law, as amended by chapter 360 of the laws of 2025, is\namended to read as follows:\n\n3c. No bonds or notes of the corporation shall be issued if upon such\nissuance the 4 aggregate principal amount of bonds and notes of the\ncorporation then outstanding exceeds the 5 lesser of (twenty) twenty-two\nbillion dollars or such amount as would cause the maximum capital\n6reserve fund requirement to exceed eighty-five million dollars;\nprovided that, in determining such 7aggregate principal amounts there\nshall be deducted (i) all sums then available for the payment of 8such\nbonds or notes either at maturity or through the operation of a sinking\nfund; (ii) the aggregate 9 principal amount of outstanding bonds issued\n(a) to refund notes and (b) to refund bonds, 10theretofore issued and\nthen outstanding; and (iii) the aggregate principal amount of outstand-\ning 11notes issued to renew notes theretofore issued and then outstand-\ning.  The provisions of the prior 12sentence notwithstanding, the corpo-\nration shall not issue bonds if such issuance shall cause the 13maximum\nreserve fund requirement to exceed thirty million dollars unless prior\nto such issuance 14 the senate and assembly shall have adopted a concur-\nrent resolution passed by the votes of a 15majority of all the members\nelected to each such house and, subsequent thereto, the governor shall\n16evidence in writing the governor's agreement with such resolution to\nthe chairperson of the 17corporation, which resolution shall be in full\nforce and effect on the date of issuance of the bonds, 18 permitting the\nmaximum capital reserve fund requirement to equal or exceed the amount\nof the 1 maximum capital reserve fund requirement which would be effec-\ntive upon the issuance of the 2 bonds in question, but in no event shall\nthe maximum capital reserve fund requirement exceed 3eighty-five million\ndollars.\n\n4 §2. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
